 "titulo": "How Spartans voted with bread 🛡️ Part 3 #history #shorts",
 "capa": "WITH IT, OR ON IT",
 "descripcion": "To join a Spartan dining group, every man dropped a ball of bread in a bowl. One flattened ball meant no. The end of your life in Sparta.\n\nSource: Plutarch, Life of Lycurgus; Sayings of Spartan Women.\n\nCould you have lasted in Sparta?\n\n#history #sparta #ancientgreece #historyfacts #shorts",
 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "A ball of bread. That's how they vote.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "The men of the table vote on you, in secret.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Each man drops soft bread into a bowl.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "A round ball means yes.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "A flattened one means no. One no, and you're out.",
   "pausa": 0.7
  },
  {
   "texto": "Because men who eat together must trust each other in battle.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "You're in. Every month, you bring barley, wine, cheese and figs.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "If you can't pay your share, you lose your place, and your rank.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Dinner is black broth, made with pork and blood.",
   "pausa": 0.7
  },
  {
   "texto": "A foreign king once tasted it, and hated it.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "A Spartan would answer: you need the exercise to enjoy it.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "After dinner, you walk home in the dark, with no torch.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "That way, you learn to move at night without fear.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then comes war. Your mother hands you your shield.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "She does not say goodbye. She says something else.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Come back with it, or on it.",
   "pausa": 0.9
  },
  {
   "texto": "You serve until sixty. Your whole life belongs to the city.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Could you have lasted in Sparta?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
